.\" Manual page for hax.
.TH HAX 1 "2026-09-23" "hax 0.5.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
hax \- minimalist terminal\-native coding agent
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B hax
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ prompt ...]
.br
.B hax
.RB { \-p | \-\-json }
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ prompt ]
.br
.B hax
.RB { \-c | \-\-resume [=\fIID\fP] }
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ prompt ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B hax
is a single small binary that acts as a coding agent in the terminal. It talks
to OpenAI, Anthropic, OpenRouter and compatible providers, to a ChatGPT/codex
account, or to local models through llama.cpp and ollama. Unlike a web chat it
runs in the native terminal scrollback, keeps the working directory as the unit
of context, reads and edits files, and runs commands as a subprocess.
.PP
It extends through configuration, markdown files and subprocesses rather than
a plugin runtime. There are no MCP marketplaces, no IDE panels, and no
per\-command permission prompts.
.PP
With no arguments
.B hax
starts an interactive REPL. In one\-shot mode the final answer goes to standard
output, while the provider banner, usage statistics, errors and the resume
hint go to standard error, so
.B "hax \-p"
is safe to pipe without losing diagnostics.
.PP
.B hax
is not a security boundary. It executes shell commands on the model's behalf
without per\-command approval. Use operating\-system\-level isolation for
untrusted work.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-print
Run non\-interactively to completion and print the final assistant message to
standard output. The prompt is taken from the positional arguments, joined with
spaces, or from standard input when no argument is given and standard input is
not a terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-json
One\-shot mode that implies
.BR \-p ,
writing the run's session records to standard output as JSON Lines, one record
per line, closed by a
.B result
record carrying the outcome, final text, usage and session id. The standard
error banner and statistics are omitted; errors and warnings still go there.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-continue
Resume the most recent conversation recorded for the current directory.
.TP
.BR \-\-resume [ =\fIID\fP]
Resume a past conversation in the current directory, restoring the provider,
model, effort and preset it last used. Without an argument a picker is shown,
which requires a terminal; with an id, or a unique prefix of one, the run
continues without prompting. A command line selection flag overrides the
restored choice and is recorded in the resumed session.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-session
Do not record this conversation. Nothing is left to resume afterwards, and
prompts are not added to the Ctrl\-R recall. Earlier sessions and prompts stay
readable.
.TP
.B \-\-raw
Send only the prompt text: no base system prompt, no environment section, no
.BR AGENTS.md ,
no skills and no tools. Useful as a barebones chat interface.
.TP
.B \-\-bare
Run without project and delegation context: no
.BR AGENTS.md ,
no skills, no subagent section. The environment section, the tools and the base
system prompt remain, unlike
.BR \-\-raw .
.TP
.BI \-\-provider= NAME
Select the backend for this run. One of
.BR codex ,
.BR openai ,
.BR anthropic ,
.BR openrouter ,
.BR opencode\-zen ,
.BR opencode\-go ,
.BR llamacpp ,
.B ollama,
or a provider defined in the configuration file.
.TP
.BI \-\-model= ID
Select the model for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-effort= LEVEL
Select the reasoning effort for this run, where the provider supports it.
.TP
.BI \-\-preset= NAME
Apply the named preset, a
.BI presets. NAME
selection from the configuration file. A preset is applied first and explicit
provider, model and effort flags are layered over it.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
The four selection flags apply to the current process only, are not persisted,
and take priority over every other source. Settings are resolved in this
order, first defined value winning:
.PP
.RS
current\-process override \(-> resumed conversation \(-> environment \(-> state file \(-> configuration file \(-> built\-in default
.RE
.SH INTERACTIVE COMMANDS
Type
.B /help
inside the REPL for the authoritative live list.
.TP
.BI /new " [" preset ]
Start a fresh conversation, optionally with a preset.
.B /clear
is an alias.
.TP
.B /resume
Pick a past session for this directory.
.TP
.BI /fork " [" n ]
Create a new session branching before an earlier prompt.
.B /fork 0
clones the current tip. Prefer it over
.B /undo
when trying an alternative, since the original session stays intact.
.TP
.BI /undo " [" n ]
Permanently truncate this session before an earlier prompt. It rewrites both
the conversation memory and the session file, and has no redo.
.TP
.B /provider
Choose a provider, model and effort.
.TP
.B /model
Choose a model and effort for the current provider.
.TP
.B /effort
Choose the reasoning effort, where supported.
.TP
.BI /preset " [" name ]
Apply a configuration\-defined preset.
.TP
.BI /preset\-save " " name " [" tint ]
Save the current provider, model and effort as a preset.
.TP
.BI /config " [" key " [" value ]]
Show the resolved value, source and description of each setting, or set one for
this process. Provider, model, effort and preset have their own commands, and
API keys are only ever reported as set or unset.
.TP
.BI /compact " [" focus ]
Summarize older context, optionally emphasising something the summary must
preserve.
.TP
.B /copy
Copy the most recent assistant response.
.TP
.BI /tasks " [" kill " " \fIid\fP... " | " kill " all ]
List background tasks, or stop them.
.TP
.B /session
Show the current session and local usage totals.
.TP
.B /usage
Query provider account or subscription usage, where supported.
.TP
.BI /login " [" provider ]
Log in to a provider account with a
.B hax\-managed
token, for ChatGPT/codex.
.TP
.BI /logout " [" provider ]
Revoke and remove a
.B hax\-managed
login.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Enter
Submit. At a paused, empty prompt, continue without adding a message.
.B Shift\-Enter
inserts a newline when the terminal sends LF for it.
.TP
.BR Up ", " Down
Recall the previous or next prompt.
.B Ctrl\-R
searches the persistent prompt history.
.TP
.B Esc
Pause after the current step so the conversation can be steered.
.B Esc
twice interrupts the model or a running tool immediately.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-C
Clear the current prompt; twice on an empty prompt quits.
.B Ctrl\-D
quits on an empty prompt.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-L
Clear the screen and redraw the prompt.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-G
Edit the prompt in
.BR $EDITOR .
.TP
.B Ctrl\-O
Open the rendered conversation in
.BR $PAGER .
This is the best view for reviewing what happened.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-T
Open the model\-facing transcript in
.BR $PAGER :
the system prompt, tool schemas, tool calls and results, and post\-compaction
context.
.TP
.B Ctrl\-V
Paste a clipboard image, or clipboard text when no image is available.
.TP
.B @ + Tab
Choose a project file with
.BR fzf (1)
and insert its path. The model reads the file only if it needs to.
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is optional: the interactive pickers work without a file and
remember provider and model choices. See
.B config.json
below for the settings reference.
.SS Files
hax follows the XDG Base Directory specification. These are the paths used
when the corresponding
.BR XDG_CONFIG_HOME ,
.B XDG_STATE_HOME
or
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
variable is unset.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hax/config.json
Durable, user\-owned configuration: defaults, provider definitions, presets and
behaviour changes. Suitable for a dotfiles repository, provided secrets stay in
environment variables. Plain JSON without comments; dotted keys are normally
nested objects.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hax/AGENTS.md
Global project instructions, loaded before any repository instructions.
.TP
.I ~/.config/hax/skills/ , ~/.agents/skills/
Skill directories containing a
.B SKILL.md
per skill.
.B <dir>/.agents/skills/
is searched first, from the current directory up to the repository root, so a
nearer directory shadows a wider one. A skill should explain when and how to use
a CLI or a repeatable workflow; project policy belongs in
.BR AGENTS.md .
.TP
.I AGENTS.md
Discovered from the repository root down to the current directory, so narrower
rules follow broader ones. Outside Git, only
.I ./AGENTS.md
is considered. This is the place for build, test, lint and formatting commands,
where important modules live, and what must not change.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hax/state.json
Remembered interactive selections, written by
.BR hax .
Do not edit by hand.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/hax/sessions/<encoded\-cwd>/
Sessions and prompt history, as JSONL, scoped to the current directory.
Sessions inactive for 30 days are removed by default; the
.B session_retention_days
setting changes that, and
.B 0
keeps them indefinitely. The format is documented in
.IR sessions.md .
.TP
.I ~/.cache/hax/catalog.json
Model metadata cache.
.SS Environment
.TP
.B HAX_PROVIDER ", " HAX_MODEL ", " HAX_EFFORT ", " HAX_PRESET
Override the provider, model, effort or preset for this run. Useful for
per\-shell and automated use; they override saved interactive choices.
.TP
.B HAX_SYSTEM_PROMPT
Replace the base system prompt.
.TP
.B HAX_SUBAGENT_DEPTH
Set by
.B hax
itself in delegated subagent processes.
.TP
.B HAX_BASH_TRANSITION_MIN_BYTES
Byte threshold above which command output is streamed progressively instead of
being returned as one record.
.TP
.BR EDITOR ", " VISUAL ", " PAGER
Used by
.BR Ctrl\-G ,
.B Ctrl\-O
and
.BR Ctrl\-T .
The two pagers default to
.B "less \-R"
when
.B PAGER
is unset.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable colour output.
.SS External programs
All of these are optional; each feature degrades gracefully without it.
.TP
.B fzf
The
.B @
file picker.
.TP
.B git
Repository context in prompts, and a faster
.B @
candidate list.
.TP
.BR less ", " more
The transcript pager.
.TP
.BR wl\-copy ", " wl\-paste ", " xclip ", " xsel
Clipboard and image paste on Wayland and X11. Without them, hax falls back to
the terminal's own OSC 52 support.
.SH PROVIDERS
.TP
.B codex
Run
.B /login
inside hax.
.TP
.B openai
Set
.BR OPENAI_API_KEY .
.TP
.B anthropic
Set
.BR ANTHROPIC_API_KEY .
.TP
.B openrouter
Set
.BR OPENROUTER_API_KEY .
.TP
.BR opencode\-zen ", " opencode\-go
Set
.BR OPENCODE_API_KEY .
.TP
.B llamacpp
Run
.BR llama\-server .
.TP
.B ollama
Run
.BR "ollama serve" .
.PP
Any OpenAI\-compatible endpoint can be added as a custom provider through the
.B providers
block of
.IR config.json .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The run finished.
.TP
.B 1
The run failed.
.TP
.B 130
A one\-shot run was interrupted by
.B SIGINT
or
.BR SIGTERM .
Completed work is saved and the session stays resumable. A second signal kills
the process.
.PP
In one\-shot mode
.B SIGUSR1
pauses cleanly at the next turn boundary instead, and reports the outcome as
.BR paused .
.SH EXAMPLES
Start a conversation in the current repository:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hax
.fi
.RE
.PP
Run a single task and capture only the answer:
.PP
.RS
.nf
answer=$(hax \-p "summarize the public API")
.fi
.RE
.PP
Keep diagnostics out of the captured result:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hax \-p "produce JSON only" >result.json 2>run.log
.fi
.RE
.PP
Observe a run as it happens:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hax \-\-json "fix the failing test" | jq 'select(.kind == "tool_call" or .type == "result")'
.fi
.RE
.PP
Continue yesterday's conversation here, on a different model:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hax \-\-resume \-\-model=other\-model
.fi
.RE
.PP
Ask a plain model question with no tools and no project context:
.PP
.RS
.nf
hax \-p \-\-raw "explain this error message"
.fi
.RE
